    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §181, Gen Muni L; amd §498, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6491\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the\ngeneral municipal law and the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to\nauthorizing the county of Rockland to regulate the registration and\nlicensing of taxicabs, limousines, and livery vehicles\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis legislation would grant Rockland County the power to\nadopt local laws or ordinances regulating taxicabs, limousines, and\nlivery vehicles.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThis bill amends section 181 of the General\nMunicipal Law and section 498 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation would correct the inequity of the\ncurrent system that prohibits taxicabs, limousines, and livery\nvehicles from Rockland County to operate in other jurisdictions but\nallows these vehicles from other jurisdictions to operate in Rockland\nCounty.\nThis legislation would also protect licensed Rockland County taxicabs,\nlimousines, and livery vehicles from being required to be licensed in\nother licensing jurisdictions, provided that the county adheres to\nthe \"reciprocity\" standards currently existing in the Vehicle and\nTraffic Law. Additionally, licensed taxicabs, limousines, and livery\nvehicles in other authorized jurisdictions would not be required to\nbe licensed in Rockland County provided that they are licensed in\njurisdictions adhering to the same \"reciprocity\" standards.\nThis will allow a vehicle licensed in Rockland County to either pick\nup or drop off a passenger in another licensed jurisdiction without\nbeing separately licensed by such other jurisdiction. It will not\nauthorize such vehicle to perform point-to-point services within such\nother licensed jurisdiction without being licensed by such other\njurisdiction.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
